{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793689088,"nonce":"gkDCh7GRK4UM5tphv0BuzZm4sTY=","message":"Scope confirmed at the start of M5a planning (2026-11-02). Decisions due at the start of M5a:\n\n- **Metavariables (design §7.1).** `Warrant.Cic.Expr` gains a metavariable case. The kernel rejects any term that contains one, as Lean's kernel does. Lean's Meta code then ports nearly line for line. Rejected alternative: a separate term type for Meta, which leaves the kernel's type untouched but duplicates substitution and traversal code.\n- **Budgets (Q8).** The kernel keeps its fuel defaults: 20M steps interactive, 100M for corpus runs. Tactics get their own fuel, and each theorem gets a 30-second wall-clock limit. Both are adjustable per project and per theorem. A unit that runs out of fuel or time fails; it is never accepted.\n- **CI trust (Q9).** M5a has no cache, so every build re-checks every proof with the kernel. Recorded as \"always recheck\" for M5a. Signed caches are decided when M5b adds the cache.\n- **Porting depth.** `simp` and `omega` port Lean 4.35.0's algorithms in the shape Lean uses, including the proof terms they produce, but only the parts the exit criterion needs. Simprocs, arithmetic normalisation and `simp?` wait. Later milestones extend this code instead of replacing it.\n- **Visual Studio.** The exit criterion includes Visual Studio's MSBuild (.NET Framework). It is checked on a machine with Visual Studio installed; where it is not installed, the check is reported as not run.\n\nOut of scope: the server, cache, store and analyzers (M5b); exceptions, contracts, `decimal` and strings (M6 and later); `decide` over finite domains, `split` and `grind`.\n\nPlan document: `docs/plans/` plus literate chapters under `docs/m5a`, as for M4. Not yet written.","files":null}]}